// ---------------------------------------------------------------- v1.174 THE SKYSCRAPER, THE LOOK (this file is spliced into template.html by build_html.py, right after tower.js; tower.js is the map's rules, this is what you see)
// Everything is pixel art made from the same few tools: SPRITES and PICTURES are drawn once and kept (a whole floor's shell, every piece of furniture, the light masks, the sky tiles), so a frame only copies them: the walls, the ceiling, the carpet and the slab you cut through are one
// picture per floor (twShell, made the first time you see the floor and thrown away after a few more floors), the furniture comes from sprites with a 3-tone shading and a dark outline (twSprite), the lights are dithered cones and glows that punch holes in a layer of darkness (twLights; the darkness
// grows with every light that breaks), the city outside is made of tiles that scroll at three speeds (twSkyDraw: dusk at the bottom, a starry night with a sea of clouds at the top, and rain, fog or a storm on some floors), and a front layer (twFront, called from drawPeds) puts dust in the
// light, a vignette and the haze of what broke over the fighters. SETTINGS > GRAPHICS decides how much of it is on (twQ: the BACKGROUND DETAIL, the GLOW; the low-quality switch takes the lights and the front layer away).
const SH_Y = 10, SH_F = 91, SH_N = 107, SH_H = 130;      // (the shell of a floor, row by row: 0 - 9 the ceiling, 10 - 90 the wall, 91 - 106 the floor, 107 - 129 the slab under it)
